From 9593fad231a4bd73a1517ba1ae1428a665adffd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:20:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: give System One calls' usage rows their bodies for
 the OTLP export
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A System One call's span carried no request or reply while a chat's
carried both: the chat path fills its usage record with withBodies
before appendUsage, and neither decide path did (#5102) — the OTLP
exporter only blanks the bodies, it never fills them.

Both paths had the exchange in hand already:

- serveDecideTries kept the request on its call; the answer is in hand
  though the client reads it only after the usage row is written, so
  the row takes it from there (the call keeps what the capture keeps
  once the reply goes out).
- systemOne built its call only for the archive, so the call outlives
  that if now and carries its request (as the provider was sent it)
  and the answer when an observer wants bodies.

Bodies follow the rules a chat's do: scrubbed as the request archive's
are, the first 256 KiB Recent calls keep, or whole when the export
wants them whole.

Pinned by TestOTelExportsSystemOneBodiesWhenOn: with bodies on, a
POST /v1/systemone and the router's own classifier call each export
langfuse.observation.input and output, as a chat's span does; with
bodies off, neither does.

